			],
			"Message": "style(Common): Remove blank lines after opening braces in TypeScript sources\n\nRemove the blank lines immediately following opening braces (`{`) in interface bodies, type declarations, export const blocks, function bodies, and between import groups across all TypeScript runtime source files, generated type declarations, and the test file. Also normalize README table formatting by adding alignment row pipes and fixing indentation on the Related Documentation list item.\n\nThis is the complementary whitespace pass to the prior \"Add separator blank lines\" commit: blank lines between logical members are kept, but blank lines directly after opening braces are removed. The effect is a tighter vertical rhythm where the content begins immediately after the opening delimiter rather than being separated by an empty line.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Source runtime files (Container.ts, EffectSmol.ts, Errors.ts, PubSub.ts, Ref.ts, Result.ts): Strip blank lines after interface opening braces, after `export const`, `export type`, and function body opening braces\n- TypeScript Interface declarations (Access, Data, Decrypt, Encrypt, Get, Object, Put, Redirect, Response, Uint8ArrayFromObject): Remove blank line after `export default interface Interface {` in both .ts and .d.ts variants\n- TypeScript Function declarations (Access.ts, Redirect.d.ts, Response.d.ts): Remove blank lines between import statements and after type declaration opening braces\n- Test file (EffectSmol.test.ts): Remove blank lines between consecutive import statements\n- README.md: Add alignment row pipes (`| --- | --- |`) to all markdown tables and fix hanging indent on the Related Documentation `CHANGELOG.md` list item\n\nImpact: Consistent whitespace cadence where blank lines separate logical blocks but do not follow opening delimiters, across all TypeScript sources in the Common crate.",
			"SHA": "abb0d2105bf87be06a16a78041236bafc5188bda"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:11:50Z",
			"File": [
