			"Message": "style(Common): Strip leading \"This\" and \"It\" from doc comment openings\n\nNormalise Rust doc comment prose across the entire Common crate to use the\nstronger, subject-led style that starts directly with \"Implemented by\",\n\"Uses the\", \"Defines\", or \"Provides\" rather than the weaker \"This trait is\nimplemented by\" or \"It uses the\" patterns.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Remove leading \"This trait/function/struct/method\" from all doc comment\n  opening sentences across 33 files in Command, Configuration, Document,\n  Effect, ExtensionManagement, FileSystem, IPC, Keybinding, LanguageFeature,\n  Secret, StatusBar, Storage, Terminal, Transport, TreeView, UserInterface,\n  Webview, and Workspace services\n- Collapse superfluous blank lines between doc comment sections (e.g., between\n  description and `# Parameters`, between `# Parameters` and its first bullet,\n  between description and `# Returns`)\n- Fix a malformed doc comment in WebviewProvider.rs where `// # Parameters`\n  used double-slash instead of triple-slash, restoring proper doc generation\n- Fix a blank-line-split doc comment opening in ExtensionManagementService.rs\n- Tighten abbreviated doc summaries: \"Represents the type of\" → \"The type of\"\n  for DTO enum docs, removing redundant meta-commentary\n\nImpact: Consistent, professional, active-voice doc comments across all\ntrait definitions and effect constructors in the Common crate.",
